trigger:
Paper today: cannot happen. A paper start has no broker check and sends no orders.

After Go Live, all of these are needed:
(1) a live trader start: pressing Go Live, the automatic start after a Mac restart, or ./jb live;
(2) the start falls in pre-market, regular hours or after-hours;
(3) a sell condition is already met at that moment (price past the 2% stop or 4% target, or overnight_gap holding into regular hours);
(4) the live record has no backup stop on file;
(5) a minute ends with a trade inside the ~1-2 s window, which is roughly 2-3% of such starts.

The short-position outcome also needs the account to hold fewer shares than the record. The most plausible way is an exit that actually filled but was marked "unconfirmed" (finding A2, e.g. around IB Gateway's nightly restart). That exit had already cancelled the backup stop, and the A2 message tells Alex to restart in exactly that state.

Not expected in a normal week. Possible over months of live trading with frequent restarts.

severityWhy:
After Go Live at IBKR this leaves a wrong position: an unintended short of a 3x ETF on margin, up to about $25k. Path (a) has a partial safety net: within about a minute a push says 'positions differ: broker says -N'. Path (b) is close to silent: the only push says 'Backup stop sold N at X', which reads like a normal protective exit, and the tab still shows the old 'broker says 0' text. Some things limit it:
- it is zero risk while paper;
- the Stop button fixes the state;
- the A1 behaviour usually cancels the stale stop at the next algo stop-loss or exit bar;
- Webull likely refuses the extra sell, which is why B rated its side MEDIUM.
The IBKR consequence matches the CRITICAL definition.

fix:
In _live, for every closing order (not only the kill switch), read _broker_shares():
- 0 or the opposite side: book 'closed outside the algo' and send nothing;
- fewer shares than the ledger: send at most that many;
- None (can't read): keep today's behaviour.
In _bstop_tick, cancel the backup stop when the broker holds fewer shares than the stop covers (seen on two reads about 10 s apart).

trigger:
Live mode only, so it cannot happen today: paper orders are simulated and never reach the unconfirmed path.

After Go Live, it needs an algo order (entry, exit or stop-loss) to be in its roughly 90 s window (cancel_after_s, default 60 s, plus 30 s) at the same moment as one of these:
- an IB Gateway disconnect: the nightly 11:50 pm ET restart, the Sunday re-login, a crash, Mac sleep or a network drop;
- IBKR losing its link (1100) so the cancel gets no answer;
- the Webull API timing out or rate-limiting for about 30 s after the cancel;
- a late fill report.

With a few orders a week this is rare (a low single-digit chance per month). It is most likely for an overnight strategy whose stop-loss fires near 11:50 pm, or on a bad Webull API day. Once it happens it lasts until Alex looks at the algo tab or phone page and restarts the trader by hand.
